# CSS Module Conventions

- Use BEM class names: `.block`, `.block__element`, and `.block--modifier`.
- Compose Tailwind utilities with `@apply`; do not duplicate utility declarations manually when an equivalent utility exists.
- Prefer Tailwind responsive variants in `@apply` (for example, `@apply md:grid-cols-2`) over handwritten `@media` blocks.
- Use `@media` only when Tailwind has no suitable responsive variant or the rule cannot be expressed with `@apply`.

```css
/* Good */
.product-card {
  @apply grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2;
}

.product-card__title {
  @apply text-lg;
}

.product-card--featured {
  @apply border-2;
}
```
